{{!
    @template local_oksigeniaeguahe/public_pegs

    The rail of the page of a family and of the sign-up, one peg per child (a wooden knob seen from the front, drawn in
    front of what hangs): what hangs for its age, the same drawings as in the panel (panel_hanging, by the ladder of
    data/escalera.json), with the name used at home written by hand. Without a course yet, as on the sign-up, the small
    backpack of the mark of Eguahe with the first-day label on its pocket (the band in the colour of the centre, one
    corner peeling up). With no name yet, the label waits blank. Once the family came (came), the label of the
    backpacks is stuck down, as at the door: its corner no longer lifted. Drawings only: the name is in the heading.

    Example context (json):
    {"count": 2, "live": false, "came": true, "pegs": [{"index": 0, "name": "Leo", "style": "--reposo:-3.5deg",
        "object": "mochila", "arriving": true, "stuck": true, "hidden": false}, {"index": 1, "name": "Ana",
        "style": "--reposo:3deg", "object": "credencial", "arriving": true, "stuck": true, "hidden": false}]}
}}
<div class="perchas n{{count}}{{#came}} pegada{{/came}}"{{#live}} data-live="1"{{/live}}>
    {{#pegs}}
    <div class="percha" data-i="{{index}}"{{#hidden}} hidden{{/hidden}}>
        {{> local_oksigeniaeguahe/panel_hanging }}
    </div>
    {{/pegs}}
</div>
